{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee","id":1499803,"title":"Where is John Dee?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-15T17:29:42-08:00","id":1499803,"title":"Where is John Dee?","content":"I mean it's been quite a while since I don't hear about him, does anybody have a clue? Any news about him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T00:08:38-08:00","id":1499842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee#post1499803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's been quite a while since I don't hear about him, does anybody have a clue? Any news about him?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty good question - as an aside, i've always been curious about how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enochian\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> part of Dee's work would fit in a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ghemalish\" target=\"_blank\">Masquerade</a> context....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-16-2022, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T10:27:28-08:00","id":1499866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499842#post1499842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pretty good question - as an aside, i've always been curious about how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enochian\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> part of Dee's work would fit in a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ghemalish\" target=\"_blank\">Masquerade</a> context....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I'm not sure if this (his Enochian studies) could be understood as dangerous to the masquerade or rather good to confuse the humans lol, in any case I miss the guy, it seems WW almost completely forgot about him after &quot;A World of Darkness&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:46:06-08:00","id":1499896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499866#post1499866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I'm not sure if this (his Enochian studies) could be understood as dangerous to the masquerade or rather good to confuse the humans lol, in any case I miss the guy, it seems WW almost completely forgot about him after &quot;A World of Darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He does get a citation as the person who got <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dylan_Bruce\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Bruce</a> in the Red List in the original Kindred Most Wanted, that he did partly due to a theory of his that <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Lady Anne</a> was somewhat responsible for his success in hunting kindred in London during the Blitz. So basically he got him there from suspecting there was more than incompetence or omission behind that and wanting the dirt to prove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-21-2023, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T13:46:06-08:00","id":1499897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499866#post1499866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I'm not sure if this (his Enochian studies) could be understood as dangerous to the masquerade or rather good to confuse the humans lol, in any case I miss the guy, it seems WW almost completely forgot about him after &quot;A World of Darkness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He does get a citation as the person who got <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dylan_Bruce\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Bruce</a> in the Red List in the original Kindred Most Wanted, that he did partly due to a theory of his that <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Lady Anne</a> was partly responsible for his success in hunting kindred in London during the Blitz.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically he got Dylan into it from suspecting there was more than incompetence or omission from Lady Anne's part behind that and wanting the dirt to prove it.<br /> <br /> Have yet to see how Dylan's rewrite/update in Dread Names, Red List and BJD affects or not Dee's own story, but based on <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gabrielle_di_Righetti\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> at least (have to check Dread Names to confirm) he was involved not only with Dylan's declaration in the 80s but his active hunt along with Justicar di Righetti. But considering the quite peculiar role <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Quaesitor_(Archon)\" target=\"_blank\">quaesitors</a>, in the service of the Camarilla... Dee's choice to join their ranks raises the possibility that Righetti, Dee or both are aware of his infernalist ties or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-16-2022, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T18:04:55-08:00","id":1499920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499897#post1499897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He does get a citation as the person who got <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dylan_Bruce\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Bruce</a> in the Red List in the original Kindred Most Wanted, that he did partly due to a theory of his that <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anne_Bowesley\" target=\"_blank\">Lady Anne</a> was partly responsible for his success in hunting kindred in London during the Blitz.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically he got Dylan into it from suspecting there was more than incompetence or omission from Lady Anne's part behind that and wanting the dirt to prove it.<br /> <br /> Have yet to see how Dylan's rewrite/update in Dread Names, Red List and BJD affects or not Dee's own story, but based on <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gabrielle_di_Righetti\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> at least (have to check Dread Names to confirm) he was involved not only with Dylan's declaration in the 80s but his active hunt along with Justicar di Righetti. But considering the quite peculiar role <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Quaesitor_(Archon)\" target=\"_blank\">quaesitors</a>, in the service of the Camarilla... Dee's choice to join their ranks raises the possibility that Righetti, Dee or both are aware of his infernalist ties or more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This part of Dylan I didn't even remember, but in BJD the only mention about &quot;him&quot;, isn't actually about him, but another John Dee. I think it's rather strange that he's basically working under di Rissole as by his original character sheet, it's hard to imagine she is above him, the guy had a quite impressive character sheet. It seems that, at the very least they heavily downplayed his importance in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T19:10:08-08:00","id":1499923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499920#post1499920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This part of Dylan I didn't even remember, but in BJD the only mention about &quot;him&quot;, isn't actually about him, but another John Dee. I think it's rather strange that he's basically working under di Rissole as by his original character sheet, it's hard to imagine she is above him, the guy had a quite impressive character sheet. It seems that, at the very least they heavily downplayed his importance in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, my first instinct was also to think of Dee as a patron hiding behind the position of subordinate.<br /> Then i compared their VtES cards. Seriously, the lady is a beast.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T19:57:06-08:00","id":1499926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499923#post1499923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, my first instinct was also to think of Dee as a patron hiding behind the position of subordinate.<br /> Then i compared their VtES cards. Seriously, the lady is a beast.....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, my first instinct was also that he was king of &quot;acting behind the scene&quot;. In any case I don't know, nor play VtES card game, but as far as I know it's not canonical and I've never heard about this lady. There are so many characters that we never more heard about again, John Dee is one, but then there's Azaneal, Thomas Wyncham, Abetorius and Oliver Thrace, the latter has one short mention in BJD, but that's all (at least I don't remember if his arc had any continuation/conclusion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 12-16-2022, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T23:04:39-08:00","id":1499931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499926#post1499926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, my first instinct was also that he was king of &quot;acting behind the scene&quot;. In any case I don't know, nor play VtES card game, but as far as I know it's not canonical and I've never heard about this lady. There are so many characters that we never more heard about again, John Dee is one, but then there's Azaneal, Thomas Wyncham, Abetorius and Oliver Thrace, the latter has one short mention in BJD, but that's all (at least I don't remember if his arc had any continuation/conclusion)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, true. Me, i like to occasionally mine VtES characters or storylines for ideas with which may seem vaguely familiar while deviating wildly from metaplot, when not cooking up homebrew aliances, rivalries or other relationships out of small bits like which series number a NPC card is part of and consequently compatible or not with.<br /> <br /> (It's one of the things that led to my own alternative take of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Constancia\" target=\"_blank\">Capuchin's </a>identity and interests for example)<br /> <br /> Having the cards at hand can also be at times a convenient springboard to fleshing out unsttated NPCs or updating less than sterling ones.<br /> Madame Guil, Wihelm Waldburg, Francois Villon, Gotsdam, Menele and a bunch of others have been of immense value on that subject. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-17-2022, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T23:41:31-08:00","id":1499932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499931#post1499931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, true. Me, i like to occasionally mine VtES characters or storylines for ideas with which may seem vaguely familiar while deviating wildly from metaplot, when not cooking up homebrew aliances, rivalries or other relationships out of small bits like which series number a NPC card is part of and consequently compatible or not with.<br /> <br /> (It's one of the things that led to my own alternative take of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Constancia\" target=\"_blank\">Capuchin's </a>identity and interests for example)<br /> <br /> Having the cards at hand can also be at times a convenient springboard to fleshing out unsttated NPCs or updating less than sterling ones.<br /> Madame Guil, Wihelm Waldburg, Francois Villon, Gotsdam, Menele and a bunch of others have been of immense value on that subject. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's actually an interesting use for the VtES cards. You got me curious there with the &quot;alternative take on the Capuchin's identity&quot;. Don't you like the idea from V20 A guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra?<br /> Nowadays I don't even know where to get VtES cards btw lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T15:03:15-08:00","id":1500201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499932#post1499932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's actually an interesting use for the VtES cards. You got me curious there with the &quot;alternative take on the Capuchin's identity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing too fancy really - but if one compares the <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/7/72/Capuchin_CbG.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140425023007\" target=\"_blank\">original art</a> of the &quot;mysterious monk&quot; in Clanbook: Giovanni.<br /> <br /> With <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/c/cf/Lady_Constancia_VTES.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140324074244\" target=\"_blank\">Constancia's </a>VtES card, it can inspire the mind to go into interesting directions - specially when one considers that not only <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Roger_de_Camden\" target=\"_blank\">Lord Camden</a> but <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ambrogino_Giovanni\" target=\"_blank\">Ambrogino</a> are cited as her childer....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499932#post1499932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you like the idea from V20 A guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the contrary, i appreciate it as a very brave and decent fix not to mention effort of refreshing the stale morass of half-baked ideas that the Capuchin-Japheth-Lazarus conspiracy theory/plotline was back in late 2nd to Revised eras.<br /> <br /> But as you can guess from the way i described its previous iteration, i overall prefer to go <b>without</b> Japheth, Lazarus or whoever playing &quot;Montano's knockoff&quot; or any other &quot;last vengeful childe of a dead antediluvian&quot; types. So a potentially much more twisted and corrupt Constancia makes a far more entertaining alternative to toy with and monkeywrench expectations of setting familiar players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1499932#post1499932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowadays I don't even know where to get VtES cards btw lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, truth be told me neither, but i do have a big library of jpg images of them for use as reference or props in game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T15:49:05-08:00","id":1500211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite the contrary, i appreciate it as a very brave and decent fix not to mention effort of refreshing the stale morass of half-baked ideas that the Capuchin-Japheth-Lazarus conspiracy theory/plotline was back in late 2nd to Revised eras. </div> </div> </div>I agree, to be sincere I think the whole book was very brave and one of the best made in V20. I like that it tackles some things in the setting that were kind of left behind and managed to deal with them in a way I find fitting and satisfying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a potentially much more twisted and corrupt Constancia makes a far more entertaining alternative to toy with and monkeywrench expectations of setting familiar players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>This is something I also enjoy, to play with my players expectations and make some of these changes to the setting. This one is quite interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, truth be told me neither, but i do have a big library of jpg images of them for use as reference or props in game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>This gave me some ideas. It's good to finally get these cards to be of some use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T05:06:03-08:00","id":1500284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500211#post1500211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, to be sincere I think the whole book was very brave and one of the best made in V20. I like that it tackles some things in the setting that were kind of left behind and managed to deal with them in a way I find fitting and satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a number of interesting ideas indeed and i appreciate it even though most of it is useless in my most recent chronicle, where the PCs coterie has been partially responsible for the &quot;loss&quot; of Enoch, sending Helena to torpor (along with a good chunk of Chicago's kindred population) and mostly recently a terrible, terrible mess involving a confrontation with Ur-Shulgi. Everybody would be in the Red List (back in one case) if doing so wasn't more trouble than its worth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500211#post1500211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I also enjoy, to play with my players expectations and make some of these changes to the setting. This one is quite interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm always messing around with bits of either metaplot or canon when STing (sometimes even as player through character background if i can get away with it) like a little mash-up of multiple editions lore on the Baali by introducing the idea of 13 Shaitans, forsworn of multiple origins that would proclaim themselves as &quot;true founders of the Baali&quot; and challenge among other things through the ages. Ur-Shulgi being the one previously know as Baal the Destroyer and the &quot;Shaitan of Cnossos&quot; (and sire of Cibele) <b>not </b>really Nergal but a Malkavian forsworn ancient, possibly one of the first, whose experiments in the period would lead among other things to the formation of the Cobweb.<br /> <br /> Tiamat and Mictlantecuhtli from the Diablerie adventures also make part of the club (Mictlan in particular also being the founder of my own homebrew version of the Harbingers of Skulls).<br /> <br /> Speaking of John Dee per se, in my games i have implied once or twice, inspired by commentaries about historical one physical description and age at the time of his passing, that the Tremere we know is not actually the same, but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Kelley\" target=\"_blank\">a longtime associate</a> of his doing something of a subtle homage and bit of misdirection against rivals that might try to exploit his true name. He will also go around as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Doe\" target=\"_blank\">John Doe</a>, as a little personal joke.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500211#post1500211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This gave me some ideas. It's good to finally get these cards to be of some use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have thrown a number of schizo lore and plot surprises related to multiple princes or archbishops for the same city among other bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T17:21:27-08:00","id":1500342,"title":"","content":"Anyway, back to the initial subject of Pontifex Johannes Dee and stuff to do with him, well....<br /> <br /> - I dare say that being Pontifex of the British Isles can be trouble aplenty. Just think about it, being not the regent of the London or just any other one chantry but having authority - and consequently <i>responsibility </i>- for <b><i>all </i></b>chantries in England, Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland and maybe Ireland proper too, with possibly one other pontifex acting as &quot;midle management&quot; per country.<br /> <br /> So Dee has to deal with keeping tabs and coordinating 3-5 pontifexes under him, dozens of regents across the isles and all kinds of internal rivalries, intrigues and external rivals/threats of varying scales these multiple chantries might have gotten deals or trouble with across the ages.<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, let's not forget Dee was embraced in the early 1600s, what while quite respectable in matters of age, leaves room for some of those regents and pontifexes to be <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Leland_of_Durham\" target=\"_blank\">less favored</a> but <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/House_of_Tremere\" target=\"_blank\">much, much older kindred</a> with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Ages:_British_Isles\" target=\"_blank\">all kinds of weird ties, secret loyalties, obsessions and agendas</a> to complicate one's unlife and watch out for.<br /> <br /> And we are are not even going into the matter of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_of_Nations\" target=\"_blank\">commonwealth</a> and how they interact(ed) with his sphere of influence and all kinds of friendships, rivalries or enmities that might crisscross the connections past and present. In retrospect i really ask myself about Dee's relations with both <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thomas_Wyncham\" target=\"_blank\">Councillor Wyncham</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Oliver_Thrace\" target=\"_blank\">Regent Thrace</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Dr. Dee's connection to the appointment of Dylan Bruce into the Red List and past role as Quaesitor can be of major relevance too - for starters, because it shows how much clout the man possesses within the halls of the Ivory Tower in the first place. Second, the fact he's a major multinational pontifex kind of makes him probably the closest thing to a <i>de facto leader of the Quaesitore</i> outside of the Justicars themselves during the late 80s and most of the 90s. So, while theoretically below them, being the top Warlock in the field means Dee was basically the blood magician equivalent of Karsh within the premisses of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Plus, his personal interest in Dylan is on itself a ready made hook, in that it gives us excuse to involve Dee, any other quaesitors, alastors or archons he might have seniority over (plus all kind of allies, contacts, pupils or pawns) into Dylan's many shenanigans as presented in both Dread Names and BJD. Just how much does Dee know or not about Dylan, Gotsdam, Tiamat - or the Book of Grave War (that first appears in Diablerie: Britain, might be said), for instance?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, those are a few ramblings that come to mind after skimming back &amp; forth on the things referenced previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-21-2022, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T04:33:24-08:00","id":1500363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500342#post1500342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, back to the initial subject of Pontifex Johannes Dee and stuff to do with him, well....<br /> <br /> - I dare say that being Pontifex of the British Isles can be trouble aplenty. Just think about it, being not the regent of the London or just any other one chantry but having authority - and consequently <i>responsibility </i>- for <b><i>all </i></b>chantries in England, Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland and maybe Ireland proper too, with possibly one other pontifex acting as &quot;midle management&quot; per country.<br /> <br /> So Dee has to deal with keeping tabs and coordinating 3-5 pontifexes under him, dozens of regents across the isles and all kinds of internal rivalries, intrigues and external rivals/threats of varying scales these multiple chantries might have gotten deals or trouble with across the ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seem to be an overestimation of the weight or difficulty of the responsibilities, duties, and challanges that this Tremere Vampire might face and have to deal with. I think he should get some definite help and/or honest advice in regard to many undertakings, projects, and matters he decides to be involved with or becomes entagled in. Vampiresses and Vampires from Clan Tremere certainly have the culture and also as well the intelectual and mental instruction, schooling, and/or preparations needed to assure this kind of aid and support.<br /> <br /> I would also say that the Tremere Hierarchy (and possibly also other groups consisting of Tremere Vampires, Tremere Ghouls, and maybe also Ducheski Revenants - like Spellbinders from House Goratrix, Anarch Tremere Kindred, or Warlocks from House Carna) also certainly has rules, laws, and logistics which are each organized with at least some considerable focus towards aiding individuals / characters / fellows / persons in the role of commanders, generals, and also of course leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T04:41:13-08:00","id":1500364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500363#post1500363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seem to be an overestimation of the weight or difficulty of the responsibilities, duties, and challanges that this Tremere Vampire might face and have to deal with. I think he should get some definite help and/or honest advice in regard to many undertakings, projects, and matters he decides to be involved with or becomes entagled in. Vampiresses and Vampires from Clan Tremere certainly have the culture and also as well the intelectual and mental instruction, schooling, and/or preparations needed to assure this kind of aid and support.<br /> <br /> I would also say that the Tremere Hierarchy (and possibly also other groups consisting of Tremere Vampires, Tremere Ghouls, and maybe also Ducheski Revenants - like Spellbinders from House Goratrix, Anarch Tremere Kindred, or Warlocks from House Carna) also certainly has rules, laws, and logistics which are each organized with at least some considerable focus towards aiding individuals / characters / fellows / persons in the role of commanders, generals, and also of course leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And it seems to me you are have limited experience with the convoluted ups and downs, back-&amp;-forth and office politics that are at the heart, for good and for ill, of being in a managerial position in business or public service. Adding immortal ravening undead with a variety of magical powers to the equation can only further complicate matters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, he will have all kinds of allies, lieutenants, contacts, pupils, pawns and underlings - those are essential to making things possible in the first place, no denying that, but they are people who may have multiple layers of interests, loyalties, passions, obsessions and so on. Departmental miscommunication, passive-agressiveness, obstrusiveness, distraction, personal rivalries in the ranks are some of the all too common headaches someone playing the role of undead boss might deal with in a nightly basis in a well-defined hierarchic chain, that without adressing people in the rungs below that might be actively sabotaging one's leadership for all kinds of reasons.<br /> <br /> Increase the <b>scale </b>involved - from city/domain to state, to national and then multinational - and well, i can see taking in that Quaesitor role as something of a sabbatical leave even. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-21-2023, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T07:01:19-08:00","id":1500370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500342#post1500342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, back to the initial subject of Pontifex Johannes Dee and stuff to do with him, well....<br /> <br /> - I dare say that being Pontifex of the British Isles can be trouble aplenty. Just think about it, being not the regent of the London or just any other one chantry but having authority - and consequently <i>responsibility </i>- for <b><i>all </i></b>chantries in England, Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland and maybe Ireland proper too, with possibly one other pontifex acting as &quot;midle management&quot; per country.<br /> <br /> So Dee has to deal with keeping tabs and coordinating 3-5 pontifexes under him, dozens of regents across the isles and all kinds of internal rivalries, intrigues and external rivals/threats of varying scales these multiple chantries might have gotten deals or trouble with across the ages.<br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, let's not forget Dee was embraced in the early 1600s, what while quite respectable in matters of age, leaves room for some of those regents and pontifexes to be <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Leland_of_Durham\" target=\"_blank\">less favored</a> but <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/House_of_Tremere\" target=\"_blank\">much, much older kindred</a> with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Ages:_British_Isles\" target=\"_blank\">all kinds of weird ties, secret loyalties, obsessions and agendas</a> to complicate one's unlife and watch out for.<br /> <br /> And we are are not even going into the matter of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonwealth_of_Nations\" target=\"_blank\">commonwealth</a> and how they interact(ed) with his sphere of influence and all kinds of friendships, rivalries or enmities that might crisscross the connections past and present. In retrospect i really ask myself about Dee's relations with both <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thomas_Wyncham\" target=\"_blank\">Councillor Wyncham</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Oliver_Thrace\" target=\"_blank\">Regent Thrace</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Dr. Dee's connection to the appointment of Dylan Bruce into the Red List and past role as Quaesitor can be of major relevance too - for starters, because it shows how much clout the man possesses within the halls of the Ivory Tower in the first place. Second, the fact he's a major multinational pontifex kind of makes him probably the closest thing to a <i>de facto leader of the Quaesitore</i> outside of the Justicars themselves during the late 80s and most of the 90s. So, while theoretically below them, being the top Warlock in the field means Dee was basically the blood magician equivalent of Karsh within the premisses of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Plus, his personal interest in Dylan is on itself a ready made hook, in that it gives us excuse to involve Dee, any other quaesitors, alastors or archons he might have seniority over (plus all kind of allies, contacts, pupils or pawns) into Dylan's many shenanigans as presented in both Dread Names and BJD. Just how much does Dee know or not about Dylan, Gotsdam, Tiamat - or the Book of Grave War (that first appears in Diablerie: Britain, might be said), for instance?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, those are a few ramblings that come to mind after skimming back &amp; forth on the things referenced previously.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Many fascinating ideas there.<br /> <br /> Well I agree with many things you said here, in fact, the fact that John Dee appointed Dylan Bruce to the Red List shows that he has indeed a great deal of influence within the Camarilla, what makes it even more strange that he's serving under another Tremere, rather than being a Justicar himself. I also wonder how much does he know about Dylan, Gotsdam and Tiamat. Gotsdam, by the way, is a character that changed a lot since the time he was introduced. He was presented at first as a rather apolitical, antisocial and eccentric Ventrue that despised social contact and just wanted to be left alone to pursue Golconda or something similar. Later he seemed much darker in the sense that it's hard to understand his real motives regarding his relationship with Dylan Bruce. It seems he is somehow playing the Jyhad, after all, despite having avoided it for his entire existence (according to the way he was first presented).<br /> <br /> Another thing your post reminded me is how terrible strange and terribly made are the character's sheet in The Ventrue Chronicle. That isn't something new regarding Dark Ages character sheets, but beyond presenting one of the weakest cast of characters in any Vampire Book I've ever read, all of them seems to have a &quot;bug&quot; or &quot;glitch&quot; because ALL THE CHARACTERS have Willpower 5 LOL, it really seems like a &quot;bug&quot;, I mean not only because I think it would be at THE VERY LEAST unfitting to have Leeland, A FORMER MAGE (and a potent one according to his bio) AND A TREMERE to have Willpower 5, but also because THEY ALL HAVE WILLPOWER 5. I mean it's clearly a &quot;bug&quot; or something or the person responsible for the character's traits had NOD IDEA about what he was doing lol.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant lol, but as an experienced storyteller and someone who love the World of Darkness so much since I was a kid, these things make me REALLY mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T06:06:54-08:00","id":1500448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500370#post1500370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Many fascinating ideas there.<br /> <br /> Well I agree with many things you said here, in fact, the fact that John Dee appointed Dylan Bruce to the Red List shows that he has indeed a great deal of influence within the Camarilla, what makes it even more strange that he's serving under another Tremere, rather than being a Justicar himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a quite simple answer actually, imho: accountability. Being a specialized archon means his position theoretically has less power but also comes with less strings attached and supporters' interests/pressures for a kindred to juggle while doing its own thing.<br /> <br /> Think about it, being a Justicar would put him in a <b>very </b>visible position with a whole variety of tradition-related responsibilities for princes and primogen all across the world to badger him about. Meanwhile, while as <i>a mere senior quaesitor</i>, Dee gets far less pressure to deal with - for a similar or potentially <b>greater </b>amount of influence through playing the role of <i>advisor </i>to not only the justicar he's technically serving but all of them.<br /> <br /> Besides, the greater part of his equals are all (lower-ranked) clanmates plus all his work load is about beating other blood magicians to steal their stuff, <b><i>how is that not better than being Justicar</i></b>?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500370#post1500370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder how much does he know about Dylan, Gotsdam and Tiamat. Gotsdam, by the way, is a character that changed a lot since the time he was introduced. He was presented at first as a rather apolitical, antisocial and eccentric Ventrue that despised social contact and just wanted to be left alone to pursue Golconda or something similar. Later he seemed much darker in the sense that it's hard to understand his real motives regarding his relationship with Dylan Bruce. It seems he is somehow playing the Jyhad, after all, despite having avoided it for his entire existence (according to the way he was first presented).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, what the good doctor actually knows or not about the many layers of Dylan's story is very interesting question indeed. Damn, a little conspiracy theory i introduced in my own games based in a number of similarities (and for extra paranoia) is that Tiamat and Mithras are either past associates, lovers - or different identities of the same ancient Ventrue blood god. Just imagine the sheer upheaval and tensions that any strong evidence, true or fabricated, of any of these links could cause throughout the British Isles and beyond? It could cause waves even in parts of Asia, if one takes in account Mithra's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Veddartha\" target=\"_blank\">supposed pedigree</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About Gotsdam, in the original adventure i'd say he's something of an example of the &quot;rootless elder&quot; in the vein of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thaddeus\" target=\"_blank\">Thaddeus</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Johann_Weltmann\" target=\"_blank\">Johann Weltmann</a>, individuals that while not tied to any one kindred court or domain and only loosely connected to a sect, may still have considerable influence by virtue of their age, power and networks of retainers and pawns &quot;out of the grid&quot; so to speak. His &quot;darkening&quot; of tone in later editions could be said to be part a reflect of that, partly a effort to create a clearer and far more tight narrative out of his being Dylan's sire (that truth be told was little beyond a continuity wink back in KMD), while adding a certain dubiousness to his relation to Tiamat - is he abused childe turned secret nemesis or a deep tier piece in a 3D chess of multigenerational manchurian candidates moved by either Llantla or the inhuman monstrosity within her? Overall, i'm of the o, one could do worse than playing him as Inconnu monitor of London, Edinburgh or both even.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500370#post1500370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing your post reminded me is how terrible strange and terribly made are the character's sheet in The Ventrue Chronicle. That isn't something new regarding Dark Ages character sheets, but beyond presenting one of the weakest cast of characters in any Vampire Book I've ever read, all of them seems to have a &quot;bug&quot; or &quot;glitch&quot; because ALL THE CHARACTERS have Willpower 5 LOL, it really seems like a &quot;bug&quot;, I mean not only because I think it would be at THE VERY LEAST unfitting to have Leeland, A FORMER MAGE (and a potent one according to his bio) AND A TREMERE to have Willpower 5, but also because THEY ALL HAVE WILLPOWER 5. I mean it's clearly a &quot;bug&quot; or something or the person responsible for the character's traits had NOD IDEA about what he was doing lol.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant lol, but as an experienced storyteller and someone who love the World of Darkness so much since I was a kid, these things make me REALLY mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, i understand all too well, how actual character sheets for NPCs in the books can be sometimes immensely frustating - due to wildly varying power levels used in VtM x VtDA/DA:V books among other things - but i don't worry overly much. I grab them as loose reference and redo things according to my preferences, sometimes tweaking disciplines or generation along the way too.<br /> <br /> All of that said, i'll be the first to admit that i'm far less familiar with the Ventrue Chronicle than with the Giovanni or Transylvania Chronicles, that i both have played and possess physical copies of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-15-2023, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T12:59:59-08:00","id":1500467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the greater part of his equals are all (lower-ranked) clanmates plus all his work load is about beating other blood magicians to steal their stuff, <b><i>how is that not better than being Justicar</i></b>?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Yes, agreed. With all being said, I think it's the most satisfying explanation for him to have accepted this position. The fact that he has less &quot;strings attached to him&quot;, gives him a good deal of freedom to act and less visibility, so that works fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, what the good doctor actually knows or not about the many layers of Dylan's story is very interesting question indeed. Damn, a little conspiracy theory i introduced in my own games based in a number of similarities (and for extra paranoia) is that Tiamat and Mithras are either past associates, lovers - or different identities of the same ancient Ventrue blood god. Just imagine the sheer upheaval and tensions that any strong evidence, true or fabricated, of any of these links could cause throughout the British Isles and beyond? It could cause waves even in parts of Asia, if one takes in account Mithra's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Veddartha\" target=\"_blank\">supposed pedigree</a>. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's very interesting to think of how much he knows about the whole story and it's also a fertile ground for stories and conspiracies. In fact, one thing that could be well explored is exactly what, if any, links does Mithras have with Tiamat. The consequence of such things would be indeed huge and great for stories. I feel it's quite unlikely that he didn't know about Tiamat moving to Great Britain, that's something too big for him to not notice, after all there are few characters with such a tight control over their domain as Mithas with the British Isles. So, the question is how much does he know about her and how does he feel about it, rather than if he knows, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About Gotsdam, in the original adventure i'd say he's something of an example of the &quot;rootless elder&quot; in the vein of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thaddeus\" target=\"_blank\">Thaddeus</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Johann_Weltmann\" target=\"_blank\">Johann Weltmann</a>, individuals that while not tied to any one kindred court or domain and only loosely connected to a sect, may still have considerable influence by virtue of their age, power and networks of retainers and pawns &quot;out of the grid&quot; so to speak. His &quot;darkening&quot; of tone in later editions could be said to be part a reflect of that, partly a effort to create a clearer and far more tight narrative out of his being Dylan's sire (that truth be told was little beyond a continuity wink back in KMD), while adding a certain dubiousness to his relation to Tiamat - is he abused childe turned secret nemesis or a deep tier piece in a 3D chess of multigenerational manchurian candidates moved by either Llantla or the inhuman monstrosity within her? Overall, i'm of the o, one could do worse than playing him as Inconnu monitor of London, Edinburgh or both even. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I understand Gotsdam supposed role in the original <i>Diablerie Britain</i>, he reminds me a bit about Angiwar, but unlike Angiwar, Gotsdam had a full character sheet with all his traits and the fact that he had Humanity 9 (!), always amazed me. One thing that comes to mind is how much &quot;scheming&quot; can a being with Humanity 9 make, what did he have in mind when embracing Dylan and how much does he know, etc. So many questions and few answers. One might argue that since he has Humanity 9, he couldn't ever contemplate the idea of helping Tiamat, or could he? I love this kind of dubiousness of character, as happens many times in the WoD. Gotsdam is surely a character that brings more questions than answers, but I like that, as David Lynch's works many times shows that it's not always necessary to provide answers, things often don't need to be explained, etc, even if we as humans often need the conventional style in narrative, that explains everything, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah, i understand all too well, how actual character sheets for NPCs in the books can be sometimes immensely frustating - due to wildly varying power levels used in VtM x VtDA/DA:V books among other things - but i don't worry overly much. I grab them as loose reference and redo things according to my preferences, sometimes tweaking disciplines or generation along the way too. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I many times only use the character sheets for NPCs in the books as loose reference myself and almost always redo them, but this book really takes the cake. It's hard to understand the reason for everyone having WP 5, among other things. Fortunately, I'm already used to not trusting the way they make character sheets in most books, so nowadays I just take a quick look at the &quot;mess&quot; they made and make the character sheets myself. By the way, Gotsdam is one of the few characters that I never felt the need to change his original character sheet, Tiamat on the other hand, has a somewhat weird chatarter sheet. <br /> <br /> In any case, what matters most to me are the stories, these are just details (unfortunately I care too much for details sometimes, as one can see on my other post about naming an antagonist in my game hahaha).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T14:17:32-08:00","id":1500771,"title":"","content":"John Dee as a Tremere kindred was erased from canon with Abraham Mellon, a 6th generation Malkavian who masqueraded as &quot;Doctor&quot; John Dee when the mortal one died (London by Night, pg. 82).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T16:56:57-08:00","id":1500971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500771#post1500771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John Dee as a Tremere kindred was erased from canon with Abraham Mellon, a 6th generation Malkavian who masqueraded as &quot;Doctor&quot; John Dee when the mortal one died (London by Night, pg. 82).<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Dee is 5th gen <b>and</b> more importantly, a number of books set in contemporary Masquerade (Dread Names, Red List, that is much more recent than London by Night and relevant to current games, included) have referenced Dee as a Tremere through the years, so <b>not at all</b>.<br /> <br /> In fact, the &quot;6th generation Malkavian who masqueraded as a mortal occultist&quot; angle might be a stealth callback/retroinsertion for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aleister_Crowley\" target=\"_blank\">another canon NPC</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-21-2023, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T17:07:03-08:00","id":1500976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500971#post1500971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except Dee is 5th gen <b>and</b> more importantly, a number of books set in contemporary Masquerade (Dread Names, Red List, that is much more recent and relevant to current games, included) have referenced Dee as Tremere through the years, so <b>not at all</b>.<br /> <br /> In fact, the &quot;6th generation Malkavian who masqueraded as a mortal occultist&quot; angle might be a stealth callback/retroinsertion for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aleister_Crowley\" target=\"_blank\">another canon NPC</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was one of those massive shifts from what Revised era attempted to, well, revise. I happen to dislike the many changes V20 did from being &quot;canon agnostic&quot; at first and then &quot;everything on V20 IS canon&quot; they did decided to do after. Hoping for V6 to settle the matter in a not &quot;i'm rewritting everything again and this is the law!&quot; but more of a subtle way towards all editions' metaplot storylines.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T17:26:19-08:00","id":1500979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500976#post1500976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that was one of those massive shifts from what Revised era attempted to, well, revise. I happen to dislike the many changes V20 did from being &quot;canon agnostic&quot; at first and then &quot;everything on V20 IS canon&quot; they did decided to do after. Hoping for V6 to settle the matter in a not &quot;i'm rewritting everything again and this is the law!&quot; but more of a subtle way towards all editions' metaplot storylines.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>The greater part of the period books are not consistent with <i>themselves </i>even, what to say of lore in other editions, so i feel completely fine with leaving Victorian Age Vampire into the &quot;alternate crypto-reality, canonicity of info up to personal ST preference&quot; file along with everything in DA:V, just in case.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on a little aside, i have gone into some ramblings about <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1500342#post1500342\">the matter of Dee's identity</a> previously, in this same topic in fact.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T17:56:20-08:00","id":1501507,"title":"","content":"First of all, it's great to have the forum back!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, the &quot;6th generation Malkavian who masqueraded as a mortal occultist&quot; angle might be a stealth callback/retroinsertion for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aleister_Crowley\" target=\"_blank\">another canon NPC</a>.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This is in fact a very interesting observation. As you mentioned, I don't see John Dee as being replaced with Abraham Mellon, but it fits perfectly with a way to reinsert &quot;Aleister Crowley&quot; into the game as you put it.<br /> <br /> The way I see it, Victorian Age: London by Night developers probably didn't like much John Dee as a character, in fact it seems they didn't like Clan Tremere as a whole as they not only almost erased the clan's relevance in London and made the funny little thing of having one of the most lackluster Tremere characters ever as London's Chantry Regent (Edward Bainbridge) and also kind of replaced all the rivalry Mithras had with the &quot;Warlocks&quot; in the British Isles with the Toreador. I remember I was appalled when I saw that the Malkavian (Abraham Mellon) was like at least 5 times as proficient with Thaumaturgy as the Tremere Regent and the original John Dee was nowhere to be seen lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T12:52:41-08:00","id":1501564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499803-where-is-john-dee?p=1501507#post1501507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see it, Victorian Age: London by Night developers probably didn't like much John Dee as a character, in fact it seems they didn't like Clan Tremere as a whole as they not only almost erased the clan's relevance in London</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider it that even if a particular group, Clan, role, rank, or organisation has relatively poor or lacking representation and portrayal in a given book / supplement, then there are still the basic \\ standard facts, details, and information which are outlined in various supplements.<br /> <br /> Valueable and important basic information can easily be found described within the <i>Corebooks</i>, is included in supplements like <i>Guide to the Camarilla</i> (or detailed in the <i>Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i>), written in <i>Midnight Siege</i>, found in <i>Elysium - the Elder Way</i>, or contained in the <i>Counsel of the Primogen</i>. And also of course the Clan Books (the <i>Toreador Revised Clanbook</i> is certainly nice, good, and interesting) can be key and valueable.<br /> <br /> They can certainly provide context, depth, concepts, and ideas in regard to better portraying / including categories and groups of Vampires, Ghouls, and Revenants (whether it would be Obertus Revenants, or Enrathi Revenants, or maybe Ducheski Revenants) who might have been given secondary or teritiary priority in a particular book \\ supplement of Vampire: the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Some books and guides might even be outright in practice relying on the storytellers and the players making honest, nice, positive, and good effort by reading, researching, including and developing the definitely basic or standard ideas, concepts, facts, and details in regard to some categories and organisations described or mentioned as being important and involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}